# Code owners — required reviewers for sensitive paths.
#
# Crossplane tenant claims: files under gitops/tenant-claims/ are the source of truth for tenant
# provisioning. ArgoCD syncs them straight to the cluster, so a merge here PROVISIONS or (on removal)
# OFFBOARDS a tenant — including its namespace, IAM roles, and ECR. Until Kyverno envelope enforcement lands
# (BACK stack Phase 4), code review is the only guardrail on claim content (team/hostnames/policyStatements).
#
# NOTE: enforcement also requires a branch-protection rule on the default branch with
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled (a GitHub repo setting, not in this file). Expand the owner below
# to the platform team handle (e.g. @asanexample/platform-admins) once it exists.
/gitops/tenant-claims/   @gangster

# Scaffolder templates: a template defines what a self-service portal run can author (and, once #281 lands,
# what can auto-merge), so template changes are platform-only — same review bar as the claim paths (ADR-062 §4).
/scaffolder/             @gangster
